---
/**
 * Legacy URL: /grading-and-excavation/ (WP page ID 89).
 *
 * Title on the old site was the long-tail "Grading and Excavation for
 * Foundations and Retaining Walls". The <h1> keeps the short form and the
 * document title keeps the long one, so the page reads well and still matches
 * what it has always ranked for.
 *
 * The full-circle-service argument is the owner's own copy.
 */
import ServiceLayout from '../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { A } from '../lib/assets';
import { withBase } from '../lib/urls';

const showcase = [
  { asset: A.kubotaTrackLoaderOnSite,
    caption: 'Kubota SVL90-2 compact track loader — CPF owns the fleet outright.' },
  { asset: A.excavatorAndLoaderStrippingFrontYard,
    caption: 'Mini excavator and track loader stripping a front yard together.' },
  { asset: A.excavatedCutForRetainingWallFooting,
    caption: 'Excavated cut for a retaining wall footing, seen from the operator seat.' },
  { asset: A.gradedSlopeWithCobbleDrainageCourse,
    caption: 'Graded slope hand-finished, with a cobble drainage course along its base.' },
  { asset: A.gradedSubgradeReadyForNewPour,
    caption: 'Old driveway broken out and the subgrade graded, ready for a new pour.' },
  { asset: A.skidSteerWorkingNarrowSideYard,
    caption: 'Skid-steer working a side yard — access is usually the constraint.' },
];

const gallery = [
  A.trackLoaderCarryingSpoilFromTrench,
  A.loaderMovingExcavatedSoilKerbside,
  A.brokenConcreteStackedForRemoval,
  A.concreteStockpiledDuringDrivewayDemolition,
  A.excavatorLiftingBrokenConcreteSlabs,
  A.barricadedDrivewayDemolitionSpoil,
];
---

<ServiceLayout
  title="Grading and Excavation"
  eyebrow="Site Work"
  intro="CPF comes fully equipped with a complete line of grading and excavation equipment. When we say we will drive your project from concept to completion, we mean it."
  description="Grading and excavation for foundations and retaining walls across Thousand Oaks, Newbury Park and Ventura County. Own fleet of tractors, excavators and dump trucks — no separate grading contractor to coordinate. CA License #878989, C-29 / C-8."
  headerAsset={A.excavatorAndLoaderStrippingFrontYard}
  serviceName="Grading and excavation for foundations and retaining walls"
  showcase={showcase}
  gallery={gallery}
  galleryHeading="Demolition, spoil handling and site clearance"
>
  <h2>Concept to completion, with our own equipment</h2>
  <p>
    Our complete fleet of grading and excavation equipment gives us the tools
    needed to perfectly prepare your property for its upcoming project. Your
    project is managed by the best in the business, from start to finish.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it matters that it is the same company</h2>
  <p>
    Preparation is everything in the world of property renovation. Many jobs
    require the deployment of various different contractors to prepare your
    property for the project to be done. At CPF, we go the extra mile to cut out
    that extra step by providing our customers with a complete full-circle
    service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our grading and excavation services make use of our complete fleet of
    tractors, excavators and dump trucks. It is us who will carry out the
    project planning process with you, and us who know what the ultimate vision
    of your project is. It only makes sense that we handle any excavation and
    grading that may be needed to prepare for laying foundation, reshaping the
    lay of your land, or anything else.
  </p>

  <h3>The part nobody photographs</h3>
  <p>
    Excavation is the work that decides whether everything after it holds. A
    <a href={withBase('/masonry/')}>retaining wall</a> fails at its footing and
    its drainage far more often than at its face, and a
    <a href={withBase('/custom-concrete-driveways/')}>driveway</a> cracks
    because of what is under it rather than what was done to the surface. Both
    of those are settled before any concrete or block arrives on site.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is also the stage where the awkward realities surface — access for the
    machine, where the spoil goes, and what is actually buried in the yard. A
    contractor who is doing the whole job has every reason to find those on day
    one rather than hand them to whoever comes next.
  </p>

  <h2>Owner supervised, fully insured</h2>
  <p>
    Heavy equipment works next to the house, the fence and the street.
    <strong>Each project is owner supervised</strong>, and CPF is
    <strong>licensed, insured and bonded</strong> under C-29 masonry and C-8
    concrete.
  </p>
</ServiceLayout>
